    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-εικίζω</span></b>  (
			Att.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰκίζω,</span> q.v.), fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
				</span></i>
			 (v.infr.), later 
				Ep.
			 also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀεικίσσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					10.401
				</span></i>
			: 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀείκισσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.545
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Med.
			, 
				Ep.
			aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀεικισσάμην</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				559
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.404
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				Ep.
			
			aor.
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀεικισθήμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.222
				</span></i>
			 :—<i>treat unseemly, injure</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ γὰρ ἐγώ σ᾽ ἔκπαγλον
				ἀεικιῶ</span>
			<i>I will do</i> thee no great <i>dishonour</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.256
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				24.22
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				54
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Med.
			 in act. sense, Il.ll.cc.</div>
